                <pb facs="0744" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1925v02/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.00/1168: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >South</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-03-06T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 6, 1925—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>26. Your Nos. 31, March 4, 4 p.m., and 32, March 5, 7 p.m. Department desires to
                    congratulate you upon success of your efforts to compose differences between
                    Panaman officials and Indians and to commend you for able handling of this
                    difficult situation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
